# ACTIVE skip-list for hosting/reconcile/reconcile.sh (see skip-list.example for
# the format). Entries here are EXCLUDED from both diff and apply.
#
# Kept in the repo on purpose: a reconcile exception should be as visible and
# reviewable as the manifests it suppresses, not a hidden file on one host.
# Every entry states why it is here and what removes it.

# --- pool worker charts: excluded until the pool actually works -------------
# Operator decision 2026-07-24 (NEX-819 rollout). These four render zero-replica
# Deployments (plus anvil/harrow/plumb PVCs) that do NOT exist live: they were
# removed in the 2026-06-27 personal-cloud YAGNI load-drop. Their values files
# say the broker's wake controller owns the replica count and scales 0->1 on
# demand — but the pool cannot currently dispatch at all: spawned hands die in
# 40-75s with no failure signal (NEX-818, repo=""/no git credential + results
# recorded against a non-existent ledger issue).
#
# So creating the scaffolding now buys nothing and spends storage. REMOVE these
# four lines once NEX-818 is fixed and the pool is dispatching again — at that
# point reconcile will create them at 0 replicas, ready for the wake controller.
anvil.values.yaml
harrow.values.yaml
keel.values.yaml
plumb.values.yaml

# --- stale model-stack manifests: excluded until rewritten ------------------
# Added 2026-08-16, together with the change that makes reconcile walk
# clusters/dmon per-file. Those twelve manifests had never been diffed (see the
# comment in reconcile.sh), so bringing them under the loop applies them for the
# first time -- and these five are STALE: robo-dog and the local model stack have
# been reworked since they were written (operator, 2026-08-16).
#
# Applying them would not merely record drift, it would ACT: each carries
# nvidia.com/gpu=1 and would scale 0->1, starting five GPU workloads from
# obsolete definitions. vllm-gemma4-vision-dmon targets cwb/gpu=dmon-5090 -- the
# GPU dMon trains on -- and gemma-ollama/gemma-vllm carry NO nodeSelector, so
# they would land on whichever node has a free GPU.
#
# REMOVE each line once that manifest has been rewritten to match the current
# stack. Deleting a line arms a real GPU deployment, so re-read it before you do.
clusters/dmon/atom/vllm-ornith.yaml
clusters/dmon/atom/vllm-qwen36.yaml
clusters/dmon/gpu/gemma-4-12b-vllm.yaml
clusters/dmon/gpu/gemma-ollama.yaml
clusters/dmon/gpu/vllm-gemma4-vision-dmon.yaml
